# Notepad File > Open (COMMDLG) with the mouse: a double click on "system" in the directory list, then
# on "windows" to go back up, a click on a file name, Cancel clicked. The reference rig cannot click
# (DOSBox-X AUTOTYPE), so the screens after the double clicks are compared with the ones the keyboard
# gave in arch311-ref run cdlg-open (Enter on the selected directory), which must be the same; the
# file name click (04-file) is not compared.
# regress: sh tools/run-fixture-test.sh notepad "$TEST" "$OUT"
# compare: cdlg-open/06.png 02-insystem.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: cdlg-open/08.png 03-back.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: cdlg-open/09.png 05-closed.png active ignore 316 228 333 261
sleep 400
key alt+f
key o
sleep 400
shotcaret shots/01-open.png
dblclick 310 173
sleep 400
shot shots/02-insystem.png
dblclick 310 157
sleep 400
shot shots/03-back.png
click 120 153
sleep 400
shotcaret shots/04-file.png
click 476 131
sleep 400
shotcaret shots/05-closed.png
quit
